From 2ab9e079f8c321fe875eb171c52cb005892af89a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ignaciopd3 <210892957+ignaciopd3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:45:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] Casa: English and Spanish texts, following the TV's
 language
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The door and gas messages were written in Spanish in the code, and the rest of Casa's strings only existed in
Spanish. English is now the default (values/) and Spanish lives in values-es/, like the launcher; Android picks the
TV's language when the app starts, so it costs nothing at run time. DoorAlerts says which message and how many
minutes, and the words come from the strings; readings follow the language ("20.3°", "66%" in English, "20,3°",
"66 %" in Spanish). The tests read the real strings.xml files: the door in both languages, and every text present in
both with the same placeholders.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
